@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il07-nouns`
IMPORT `il07-refusals`
IMPORT `ito-il03-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-120b-indexation`
IMPORT `ito-121-individual-rates`
IMPORT `ito-121b-additional-tax`

-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07 adapter for row IL-03: Income Tax Ordinance ss 120B, 121, 121B.
--
-- Imports this row's nouns and refusals and IL-03's modules, and no other row.
-- Exposes numbers. IL-03's `A problem with the facts` (a LEFT) becomes a named
-- refusal here, because IL-06 declares a different type of the same name
-- (RECONCILE.md, clash N4) and the pipeline must see neither.
--
-- THE EARNER AS IL-03 SEES IT (input conventions): one item of income, the
-- year's salary (twelve times the monthly salary, NOTES.md fork K1), which is
-- income from employment: from personal exertion (ITO s 1), under s 2(2),
-- charged at the s 121 rates, with no duty of books unmet and no inflationary
-- amount; no sale of real estate.
--
-- VERSION 0.2.0: the rules whose names say "on a taxable income of" take the
-- year's income from the pipeline, which, where ITO s 65 governs, is row IL-08's
-- income charged in the registered spouse's name; the rules "on the earner's
-- salary" are those rules at twelve times the monthly salary, as before.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 adapter — row IL-03`

§§ `The earner, as IL-03's individual in a tax year`

GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year`
`IL-03: the earner in the tax year, in` h MEANS
    `IL-03: the earner in the tax year, with a taxable income of` (12 TIMES h's `the earner`'s `the earner's monthly salary`) `, in` h

GIVEN `the income` IS A NUMBER
      h            IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year`
`IL-03: the earner in the tax year, with a taxable income of` `the income` `, in` h MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                       IS h's `the year of the month`
        `date of birth`                  IS h's `the earner`'s `the earner's date of birth`
        `items of income`                IS LIST (`An item of income` WITH
            `amount`                                                               IS `the income`
            `from personal exertion`                                               IS TRUE
            `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS TRUE
            `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS TRUE
            `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS FALSE
            `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS 0)
        `sales of rights in real estate` IS EMPTY

§§ `Section 121 and section 121B`

@ref ITO s 121 (row IL-03, ito-121-individual-rates.l4)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-03: the tax under section 121 on the earner's salary, in` h MEANS
    `IL-03: the tax under section 121 on a taxable income of` (12 TIMES h's `the earner`'s `the earner's monthly salary`) `, in` h

@ref ITO s 121 (row IL-03, ito-121-individual-rates.l4)
GIVEN `the income` IS A NUMBER
      h            IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-03: the tax under section 121 on a taxable income of` `the income` `, in` h MEANS
    CONSIDER `the tax under section 121 for` (`IL-03: the earner in the tax year, with a taxable income of` `the income` `, in` h)
    WHEN LEFT  p THEN `IL-03 reports that the facts cannot describe a case: an amount is negative`
    WHEN RIGHT t THEN t

@ref ITO s 121B (row IL-03, ito-121b-additional-tax.l4)
GIVEN h            IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      `the amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-03: the additional tax under section 121B on the earner's salary, in` h `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount` MEANS
    `IL-03: the additional tax under section 121B on a taxable income of` (12 TIMES h's `the earner`'s `the earner's monthly salary`) `, in` h `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount`

@ref ITO s 121B (row IL-03, ito-121b-additional-tax.l4)
GIVEN `the income` IS A NUMBER
      h            IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      `the amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-03: the additional tax under section 121B on a taxable income of` `the income` `, in` h `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the additional tax under section 121B for` (`IL-03: the earner in the tax year, with a taxable income of` `the income` `, in` h) `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount`
    WHEN LEFT  p THEN `IL-03 reports that the facts cannot describe a case: an amount is negative`
    WHEN RIGHT t THEN t

§§ `Section 120B — the credit-point amount in force`

-- s 120B(e)(1) fixes the amounts of 2025, 2026 and 2027 at their 1 January 2024
-- figure after rounding, and IL-03's rule for those years reads nothing else.
-- Its record still has the fields the other years need; the capstone has no
-- figure for them and supplies a named refusal, which is never reached for a
-- year (e)(1) fixes (fields are read lazily) and is reached, by name, for any
-- other year.
@ref ITO s 120B(a), (e)(2) (source lines 4338, 4345): figures the capstone does not hold
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-07 holds no s 120B figure other than the 1 January 2024 amount after rounding, which is all s 120B(e)(1) reads for tax years 2025 to 2027` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-07 holds no s 120B figure other than the 1 January 2024 amount after rounding, which is all s 120B(e)(1) reads for tax years 2025 to 2027"

@ref ITO s 120B (row IL-03, ito-120b-indexation.l4)
GIVEN `the tax year`                   IS A NUMBER
      `the 1 January 2024 amount`      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-03: the credit-point amount in force in tax year` `the tax year` `, given the 1 January 2024 amount after rounding of` `the 1 January 2024 amount` MEANS
    `s 120B — the amount in force in the tax year` (`An amount on 1 January of a tax year` WITH
        `kind`                                                          IS `the amount of a credit point`
        `tax year`                                                      IS `the tax year`
        `amount on 1 January of the previous tax year, before rounding` IS `IL-07 holds no s 120B figure other than the 1 January 2024 amount after rounding, which is all s 120B(e)(1) reads for tax years 2025 to 2027`
        `readings for the previous tax year`                            IS `IL-07 holds no s 120B figure other than the 1 January 2024 amount after rounding, which is all s 120B(e)(1) reads for tax years 2025 to 2027`
        `amount on 1 January 2024, before rounding`                     IS `IL-07 holds no s 120B figure other than the 1 January 2024 amount after rounding, which is all s 120B(e)(1) reads for tax years 2025 to 2027`
        `amount on 1 January 2024, after rounding`                      IS `the 1 January 2024 amount`)

§§ `The ceilings, for the tests`

@ref ITO s 121 (row IL-03, ito-121-individual-rates.l4)
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-03: the top of the reduced-rate 20% band in tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    (`the section 121 ceilings for tax year` `the tax year`)'s `top of the reduced-rate 20% band`

@ref ITO s 121 (row IL-03, ito-121-individual-rates.l4)
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-03: the top of the reduced-rate 31% band in tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    (`the section 121 ceilings for tax year` `the tax year`)'s `top of the reduced-rate 31% band`
